Restore the audio.cpp fork's two-sided broadcast on binary ops and scale.

Upstream lets only src1 broadcast into a binary op and requires src0 to already
match dst; the fork lets BOTH operands broadcast up to dst, and lets scale's
src0 broadcast up to dst. The framework graph optimizer depends on the relaxed
form: it folds add(repeat(row, full), col) to add(row, col) and
scale(repeat(x, full)) to scale(x), leaving dst at the repeated shape and the
broadcast to the kernel. Without this, those folds emit graphs no backend can
execute and encoder_module_test aborts on
GGML_ASSERT(ggml_can_repeat(src1, src0) && ggml_are_same_shape(src0, dst)).

The ops.cpp hunk also picks up the fork's nb01 fix in the scale bias branch,
where upstream indexes src0 with dst's nb1 -- harmless only while same-shape
guarantees they match, which is exactly what this patch stops guaranteeing.

Both CUDA paths are separate kernels rather than edits to the tuned upstream
fast paths, so a future ggml upgrade does not have to re-merge them.

Covered by tests/unittests/test_encoder_modules.cpp.

